Example 1
Input: $fs = "dir\n\tsubdir1\n\t\tsubsubdir1\n\tsubdir2"
Output: 0

There are no files in the system (a file must contain a . character
separating a name and extension).
Since there are no files, the answer is 0.

Example 2
